// Independent proof of impossibility by rules 1–3 alone: some run of days where, even working
// every day leave allows with a rest day after each 5, the team can't fill 2 shifts a day or
// the nurses 1 a day. Brute force over every window and every person's best pattern.
function shortWindow(team, ds) {
  const most = (p, from, to) => { // most shifts p can work in ds[from..to] under rules 2 and 3
    let best = 0, streak = 0;
    for (let t = from; t <= to; t++) { if (!p.leave.has(ds[t]) && streak < 5) { streak++; best++; } else streak = 0; }
    return best;
  };
  for (let s = 0; s < ds.length; s++) {
    for (let e = s; e < ds.length; e++) {
      const len = e - s + 1;
      const all = team.reduce((a, p) => a + most(p, s, e), 0);
      const nurses = team.reduce((a, p) => a + (p.role === 'nurse' ? most(p, s, e) : 0), 0);
      if (all < 2 * len || nurses < len) return `${ds[s]}..${ds[e]}`;
    }
  }
  return null;
}
{
